Hello Everyone,
This scenario based question was asked in the KPMG interview for Azure Data Engineer Role:

“You need to process 500 GB of data daily from Azure Data Lake to Delta Lake. How would you choose the right Databricks cluster?”

Here is how I would approach it:

1. Choose the Right Cluster Type

Databricks provides two main cluster types:
 1. All-Purpose Cluster – Used for interactive workloads but expensive
 2. Job Cluster – Best for scheduled ETL jobs since it automatically terminates after execution

For this scenario, I would choose a Job Cluster to optimize costs and ensure efficiency.

2. Select the Appropriate Cluster Mode

Databricks offers different cluster modes, and the right choice depends on the workload:
 1. Standard Mode – Best for large-scale ETL jobs
 2. High Concurrency Mode – Suitable when multiple users need to run queries but not needed here
 3. Single Node Mode – Designed for small jobs, but 500 GB is too large for this

For processing 500 GB daily, Standard Mode is the best option.

3. Pick the Right Compute Resources

The choice of virtual machines impacts the performance and efficiency of data processing:
 1. Memory-Optimized VMs (E-Series in Azure) – Best for handling large datasets
 2. Compute-Optimized VMs (F-Series in Azure) – Designed for CPU-heavy tasks but not ideal for this scenario

I would select Memory-Optimized E-Series VMs for smoother data processing.

4. Configure Worker Nodes and Autoscaling

To efficiently process 500 GB of data, I would:
 1. Start with four worker nodes (Minimum Workers: 4, Maximum Workers: 8)
 2. Enable autoscaling to dynamically adjust resources based on workload
 3. Monitor job performance and fine-tune the configuration as needed

5. Enable Photon for Performance Optimization

Photon-accelerated clusters significantly improve performance for ETL jobs, especially when working with Delta Lake. Enabling Photon helps process data faster and reduces execution time.

6. Optimize Costs Using Spot Instances

To reduce costs, I would:
 1. Use Spot Instances, which are significantly cheaper than on-demand instances
 2. Enable Fallback to On-Demand Instances to prevent job failures in case of spot interruptions

7. Final Cluster Configuration
 • Cluster Type: Job Cluster
 • Cluster Mode: Standard
 • VM Type: Memory-Optimized (E-Series)
 • Min Workers: 4, Max Workers: 8
 • Autoscaling: Enabled
 • Photon Acceleration: Enabled
 • Spot Instances: Enabled with fallback option

